// Package slipspace.detect.v1 is the SlipSpace Arbiter <-> detector contract.
//
// One contract, both transports, identical shape for PII, injection, and
// toxicity (ADR-014). Variation between detector families is in values, never
// structure: every response is a list of findings, and a finding's span is
// optional — a null span means the finding applies to the whole unit, which is
// how sequence detectors (injection, toxicity) fit a span-oriented schema
// alongside span detectors (PII).
//
// Transport this release is protojson over HTTP (async). The gRPC service is
// defined here so the IDL is shape-locked (invariant #5); its server arrives
// with the deferred inline path. Detectors stay dumb: they return score +
// raw_label only, never a decision or risk level — Arbiter owns the verdict
